{"authored" [{"question" "q-317320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨1,0,2⟩$, $b=⟨3,1,0⟩$ and $c=⟨4,2,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(1\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 2)\\,-\\,0\\,(3\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 4)\\,+\\,2\\,(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =1\\,(5)\\,-\\,0\\,(15)\\,+\\,2\\,(2) \\\\  & =5+0+4 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fae40cd04e4e1c69e8a0e56e457e0e2bc2a1d4d365105fc1daf64e5b26622205" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317320" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $b\\cdot (a\\times c)$, if $4a\\cdot (-b\\times c)=12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a\\cdot (-b\\times c) & =12 \\\\ 4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =12 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fae40cd04e4e1c69e8a0e56e457e0e2bc2a1d4d365105fc1daf64e5b26622205" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a)$, if $b\\times c=⟨3,-1,2⟩$ and $a=⟨4,-2,6⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨4,-2,6⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12+2+12 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fae40cd04e4e1c69e8a0e56e457e0e2bc2a1d4d365105fc1daf64e5b26622205" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-24"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-26"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-28"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "26"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-26"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf5aa86fdcdd94a1768483bd465abfa0c3770e541187410f1c32d0943f72efb2" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-3,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -1,0,5 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 1,2,3 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/example-4347.json" "file_sha256" "d4705456f237f065369fffd00b9c0e532f7ab38c6c7219209b6eb1c0b6db3770" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 2)i-(-1\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 1)j+(-1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-10i+8j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-10,8,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨2,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-10,8,-2⟩ \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-10)+(-3)\\cdot 8+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/example-4347.json" "file_sha256" "d4705456f237f065369fffd00b9c0e532f7ab38c6c7219209b6eb1c0b6db3770" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,2,-1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,-1,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/example-4348.json" "file_sha256" "922b032e0f89f05a5503894e6de4b750b9c2bb1ae6d144bfcb1284c21d61e247" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (2\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\cdot (0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))+(-1)\\cdot (0\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =20-2-2 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/example-4348.json" "file_sha256" "922b032e0f89f05a5503894e6de4b750b9c2bb1ae6d144bfcb1284c21d61e247" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}),$ if $2\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times 3\\mathbf{c}) = 5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/example-4349.json" "file_sha256" "1604454f39a58ed2126a0d96d9da93bc5198700e121d1c5cca06e2b7d004d468" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a\\cdot (b\\times 3c) & =5 \\\\ 2\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times 3c)] & =5 \\\\ 2\\cdot 3\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =5 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a) & =-\\frac{5}{6},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b) & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/example-4349.json" "file_sha256" "1604454f39a58ed2126a0d96d9da93bc5198700e121d1c5cca06e2b7d004d468" "basis" 1387 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-317304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨0,\\,5,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨7,\\,-2,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨0,\\,5,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩\\cdot ⟨7,\\,-2,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩ \\\\  & =(0)(7)+(5)(-2)+(\\sqrt{11})(\\sqrt{11}) \\\\  & =0-10+11 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-317304" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317304" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $a=⟨-2,4,3⟩,$ $b=⟨-1,3,2⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,-1,4⟩,$ find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using the definition of the scalar triple product." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 4-2\\cdot (-1))i-((-1)\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 2)j+((-1)\\cdot (-1)-3\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =14i+8j-5k \\\\  & =⟨14,8,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-2,4,3⟩\\cdot ⟨14,8,-5⟩ \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 14+4\\cdot 8+3\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-73458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-11"] ["math" "-14"] ["math" "-15"] ["math" "28"] ["math" "32"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-11"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $a=⟨-2,0,-1⟩,$ $b=⟨-2,-1,0⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,1,4⟩,$ find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using the definition of the scalar triple product." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 1)i-((-2)\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3)j+((-2)\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =-4i+8j+k \\\\  & =⟨-4,8,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-2,0,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,8,1⟩ \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-4)+0\\cdot 8+(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-73459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5"] ["mat