_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-20063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "20"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-20063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨\\sqrt{7},-2,5⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨\\sqrt{7},3,-1⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨\\sqrt{7},-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨\\sqrt{7},3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{7})(\\sqrt{7})+(-2)(3)+(5)(-1) \\\\  & =7-6-5 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-317302" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317302" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-20050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨1,3,2⟩$, $b=⟨3,4,1⟩$ and $c=⟨2,0,1⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-20050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1)-3(3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1)+2(3\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =4-3-16 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-20050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-20050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-20050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-14"] ["math" "-15"] ["math" "-17"] ["math" "-19"] ["math" "17"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-20050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2,1,3⟩$, $b=⟨1,4,0⟩$ and $c=⟨6,-1,2⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\,(4\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,1\\,(1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 6)\\,+\\,3\\,(1\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =2\\,(8)\\,-\\,1\\,(2)\\,+\\,3\\,(-25) \\\\  & =16-2-75 \\\\  & =-61.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-317319" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317319" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-61"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨4,0,-2⟩$ and $c=⟨5,6,1⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(0\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 6)\\,-\\,2\\,(4\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 5)\\,+\\,3\\,(4\\cdot 6-0\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =1\\,(12)\\,-\\,2\\,(14)\\,+\\,3\\,(24) \\\\  & =12-28+72 \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-317317" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317317" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "56"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨1,0,2⟩$, $b=⟨3,1,0⟩$ and $c=⟨4,2,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(1\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 2)\\,-\\,0\\,(3\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 4)\\,+\\,2\\,(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =1\\,(5)\\,-\\,0\\,(15)\\,+\\,2\\,(2) \\\\  & =5+0+4 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-317320" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317320" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-128347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨7,4,9⟩,$ $q=⟨1,2,-2⟩$ and $r=⟨3,0,5⟩.$ Find $q\\cdot (r\\times p).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-128347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $q\\cdot (r\\times p)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $q,$ $r,$ and $p.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot (r\\times p) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4 & 9\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 9\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 9\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 9-4\\cdot 5)-2(3\\cdot 9-7\\cdot 5)-2(3\\cdot 4-7\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-20+16-24 \\\\  & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-128347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-128347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-128347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-20"] ["math" "-28"] ["math" "-60"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "20"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-128347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-28"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a)$, if $b\\times c=⟨3,-1,2⟩$ and $a=⟨4,-2,6⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨4,-2,6⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12+2+12 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-24"] ["math" "-26"] ["math" "-28"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "26"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-73470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-26"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-128352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $c\\cdot (a\\times b),$ if $a\\cdot ((-3b)\\times (-7c))=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-128352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot ((-3b)\\times (-7c)) & =7 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot (-7)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =7 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a) & =-\\frac{1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b) & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-128352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-128352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-128352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-128352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $b\\cdot (a\\times c)$, if $4a\\cdot (-b\\times c)=12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a\\cdot (-b\\times c) & =12 \\\\ 4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =12 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-18658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :