-20057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-20057" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-20057" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-20057" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $b\\cdot (c\\times a),$ if $b\\times c=⟨4,-1,6⟩$ and $a=⟨2,3,-1⟩.$\n\n$b\\cdot (c\\times a)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨2,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-1,6⟩ \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =8-3-6 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (c\\times a)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d81c2153284852437b84baf78a563e422a8a9ae5e7f3b1e5ee91604466b8fc24"} {"question" "q-317343" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "q-317343" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f339bcea2fc4658aac4b0b47e933f5c0ae161894cf7790beb051e3bee99a941"} {"question" "e-4347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-3,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -1,0,5 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 1,2,3 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/example-4347.json" "file_sha256" "e4eff5af3268e8de87fe759c0cc1afd5534fcbb59ca20d1c4746bfec86358c15"} {"question" "e-4347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 2)i-(-1\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 1)j+(-1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-10i+8j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-10,8,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨2,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-10,8,-2⟩ \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-10)+(-3)\\cdot 8+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/example-4347.json" "file_sha256" "e4eff5af3268e8de87fe759c0cc1afd5534fcbb59ca20d1c4746bfec86358c15"} {"question" "e-4348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,2,-1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,-1,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/example-4348.json" "file_sha256" "d96bfb167c379cc4f366ee79218feb8737680185bb5e45dd13e9d55f2eb13a44"} {"question" "e-4348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (2\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\cdot (0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))+(-1)\\cdot (0\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =20-2-2 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/example-4348.json" "file_sha256" "d96bfb167c379cc4f366ee79218feb8737680185bb5e45dd13e9d55f2eb13a44"} {"question" "e-4349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}),$ if $2\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times 3\\mathbf{c}) = 5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/example-4349.json" "file_sha256" "bff244802f86d93b47c605a436fd7749b7a24aa453a9397c002f345caa5f3134"} {"question" "e-4349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a\\cdot (b\\times 3c) & =5 \\\\ 2\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times 3c)] & =5 \\\\ 2\\cdot 3\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =5 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a) & =-\\frac{5}{6},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b) & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045951/example-4349.json" "file_sha256" "bff244802f86d93b47c605a436fd7749b7a24aa453a9397c002f345caa5f3134"}] "usage" {"e-4348" [] "q-20063" [] "e-4347" [] "q-18658" [] "q-317320" [] "q-73470" [] "e-4349" []} "basis" 1681 "retractions" [[17592186106055 :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} )$ given that $\\mathbf{a} = \\langle  1 , 0 , 2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} = \\langle  - 2 , 1 , 8 \\rangle  .$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186102568 17592186102569 17592186102570 17592186102571 17592186102572 17592186304214 17592186304215 17592186304216 17592186304217 17592186304218 17592186304254 17592186304255 17592186304268 17592186304269 17592186304270 17592186304271 17592186304272] "immutable_fields" [[17592186102567 :answer-field/correct] [17592186102567 :answer-field/id] [17592186102567 :answer-field/key] [17592186102567 :answer-field/type] [17592186304213 :answer-field/correct] [17592186304213 :answer-field/id] [17592186304213 :answer-field/key] [17592186304213 :answer-field/type] [17592186304253 :answer-field/correct] [17592186304253 :answer-field/id] [17592186304253 :answer-field/key] [17592186304253 :answer-field/type] [17592186304267 :answer-field/correct] [17592186304267 :answer-field/id] [17592186304267 :answer-field/key] [17592186304267 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
